---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="隐私政策 · Privacy Policy · readto"
  description="readto 隐私政策：我们不收集你的阅读历史，标注主要在你的浏览器本地完成。"
>
  <SiteHeader current="privacy" />

  <main class="mx-auto max-w-[880px] px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
    <header class="border-b border-readto-rule pb-10">
      <p class="mb-6 text-[13px] text-readto-muted" data-i18n="privacy.badge">隐私政策 · Last updated 2026-04-24</p>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-[40px] font-normal leading-[1.06] tracking-[-0.032em] text-readto-fg sm:text-[64px]" data-i18n="privacy.heroTitle">我们不收集你的阅读历史。</h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-[720px] text-[16px] leading-[1.85] text-readto-fg-2 sm:text-[18px]">
        <span data-i18n="privacy.heroBody">readto 的标注体验主要发生在你的浏览器本地：根据英语水平给网页里的生词加中文小注。我们不运营阅读历史服务器，不建立账号系统，也不统计你读过哪些页面。</span>
      </p>
    </header>

    <article data-lang-block="zh" class="policy-doc space-y-10 py-10">
      <section>
        <h2>简明说明</h2>
        <p>readto 是一个 Chrome 浏览器扩展。它会根据你选择的英语水平，在浏览英文网页时，为超过该水平的生词显示简洁中文小注。标注过程主要在你的浏览器里完成，readto 不通过自有服务器读取或保存你正在浏览的页面内容。</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>我们不收集什么</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>你阅读过的网页 URL 或网页正文内容；</li>
          <li>阅读历史、点击流或使用统计；</li>
          <li>广告标识、分析 SDK 或追踪数据；</li>
          <li>账户资料——readto 目前没有账号系统。</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>扩展在你的设备上保存什么</h2>
        <p>扩展使用 Chrome 原生 <code>chrome.storage</code> 保存少量设置，包括英语水平、标注偏好，以及你主动配置的 LLM 连接信息。</p>
        <p>如果你填写 API 地址、API Key 和模型名称，这些凭证只用于你的浏览器直接请求你选择的 LLM 服务，不会发送给 readto。</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>第三方服务</h2>
        <p>readto 采用 Bring Your Own Key 模式。如果你启用 LLM 翻译，请求会从你的浏览器直接发送到你配置的服务，中间不经过 readto 服务器。播放发音时，扩展可能请求公共词典服务获取单词音频；只会发送单词本身。</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>权限说明</h2>
        <p><code>storage</code> 用于保存扩展设置；<code>&lt;all_urls&gt;</code> 用于在英文网页中注入标注脚本。标注在你的设备上运行，网页内容不会发送给 readto。</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>如何删除数据</h2>
        <p>卸载扩展会清除扩展的本地存储。你也可以在选项页清空 API Key 字段来移除凭证。由于 readto 不运营阅读历史服务器，我们没有可供删除的服务端阅读数据。</p>
      </section>
    </article>

    <article data-lang-block="en" class="policy-doc space-y-10 py-10">
      <section>
        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <p>readto is a Chrome extension that annotates English words above your level with short Chinese glosses while you browse. Annotation mainly happens inside your own browser. readto does not run a server that reads or stores the pages you visit.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What we don’t collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>We don’t collect the URLs or body text of pages you read.</li>
          <li>We don’t upload your reading history, click stream, or usage statistics.</li>
          <li>We don’t embed analytics, advertising identifiers, or tracking SDKs.</li>
          <li>readto has no account system, so we don’t know who you are.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What the extension stores on your device</h2>
        <p>The extension uses Chrome’s native <code>chrome.storage</code> API to keep a small set of settings, including your English level, annotation preferences, and any LLM connection details you choose to provide.</p>
        <p>If you provide an endpoint, API key, and model name, those credentials are used only by your browser to talk directly to your chosen LLM service. They are not sent to readto.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Third parties</h2>
        <p>readto is Bring Your Own Key. When LLM translation is enabled, requests go directly from your browser to the endpoint you configured, with no readto server in between. Pronunciation playback may request a public dictionary service for audio; only the word itself is sent.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Permissions</h2>
        <p><code>storage</code> persists extension settings. <code>&lt;all_urls&gt;</code> lets the extension inject the annotation script into English webpages. Annotation runs on your device; page contents are not sent to readto.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
        <p>Uninstalling the extension clears its local storage. You can also clear the API key field on the options page to remove credentials. Because readto does not run a reading-history server, there is no server-side reading data for us to delete.</p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>
